-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: section 203 (business combinations with interested stockholders).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. The seat layer is dg3-seat.l4.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550),
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is a slice of line N of that file; an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- Section 203 is among those that section 114(b)(2) takes out of the stockholder-to-member reading of section 114(a).
-- The definitions in subsection (c) are "as used in this section only"; they are encoded here, under this section, as rules from facts.
-- Percentages of voting stock are percentages of the votes of that stock (subsection (c)(8)): every count below is a count of votes.
-- A time of day is not carried: "the time that such stockholder became an interested stockholder" is taken as a day (Fork F13 in NOTES.md).
-- Out of range: section 103 (dg1), section 251(f) and (g) (dg6), the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (the meaning of a national securities exchange: a stated fact).

-- The two absolute dates the section's rules depend on.
-- src:642 | The corporation, by action of its board of directors, adopts an amendment to its bylaws within 90 days of February 2, 1988, expressly electing not to be governed by this section, which amendment shall not be further amended by the board of directors;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(2) (src:642)
`s 203(b)(2) the day the section is dated from for the 1988 bylaw election` MEANS YMD 1988 2 2

-- src:659 | was the owner of 15% or more of the outstanding voting stock of the corporation at any time within the 3-year period immediately prior to the date on which it is sought to be determined whether such person is an interested stockholder, and the affiliates and associates of such person; provided, however, that the term “interested stockholder” shall not include (x) any person who (A) owned shares in excess of the 15% limitation set forth herein as of, or acquired such shares pursuant to a tender offer commenced prior to, December 23, 1987, or pursuant to an exchange offer announced prior to the aforesaid date and commenced within 90 days thereafter and either (I) continued to own shares in excess of such 15% limitation or would have but for action by the corporation or (II) is an affiliate or associate of the corporation and so continued (or so would have continued but for action by the corporation) to be the owner of 15% or more of the outstanding voting stock of the corporation at any time within the 3-year period immediately prior to the date on which it is sought to be determined whether such a person is an interested stockholder or (B) acquired said shares from a person described in item (A) of this paragraph by gift, inheritance or in a transaction in which no consideration was exchanged; or (y) any person whose ownership of shares in excess of the 15% limitation set forth herein is the result of action taken solely by the corporation; provided that such person shall be an interested stockholder if thereafter such person acquires additional shares of voting stock of the corporation, except as a result of further corporate action not caused, directly or indirectly, by such person. For the purpose of determining whether a person is an interested stockholder, the voting stock of the corporation deemed to be outstanding shall include stock deemed to be owned by the person through application of paragraph (9) of this subsection but shall not include any other unissued stock of such corporation which may be issuable pursuant to any agreement, arrangement or understanding, or upon exercise of conversion rights, warrants or options, or otherwise.
-- src:659 | December 23, 1987, or pursuant to an exchange offer announced prior to the aforesaid date and commenced within 90 days thereafter and either (I) continued to own shares in excess of such 15% limitation or would have but for action by the corporation or (II) is an affiliate or associate of the corporation and so continued (or so would have continued but for action by the corporation) to be the owner of 15% or more of the outstanding voting stock of the corporation at any time within the 3-year period immediately prior to the date on which it is sought to be determined whether such a person is an interested stockholder or (B) acquired said shares from a person described in item (A) of this paragraph by gift, inheritance or in a transaction in which no consideration was exchanged; or (y) any person whose ownership of shares in excess of the 15% limitation set forth herein is the result of action taken solely by the corporation; provided that such person shall be an interested stockholder if thereafter such person acquires additional shares of voting stock of the corporation, except as a result of further corporate action not caused, directly or indirectly, by such person. For the purpose of determining whether a person is an interested stockholder, the voting stock of the corporation deemed to be outstanding shall include stock deemed to be owned by the person through application of paragraph (9) of this subsection but shall not include any other unissued stock of such corporation which may be issuable pursuant to any agreement, arrangement or understanding, or upon exercise of conversion rights, warrants or options, or otherwise.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(5) (src:659)
`s 203(c)(5) the day before which the 1987 tender offers and exchange offers must have begun` MEANS YMD 1987 12 23

§ `Section 203(a): the bar for 3 years, and the three exceptions`

-- The facts about a business combination with an interested stockholder, for subsection (a).
-- src:636 | Notwithstanding any other provisions of this chapter, a corporation shall not engage in any business combination with any interested stockholder for a period of 3 years following the time that such stockholder became an interested stockholder, unless:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(a) (src:636)
DECLARE `s 203(a) Facts about a business combination with an interested stockholder` HAS
    `the day the stockholder became an interested stockholder`                                                     IS A DATE
    `the day of the business combination`                                                                          IS A DATE
    `prior to such time the board of directors approved the business combination`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `prior to such time the board of directors approved the transaction which resulted in the stockholder becoming an interested stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the votes of the voting stock that the interested stockholder owned upon consummation of the transaction`     IS A NUMBER
    `the votes of the voting stock of the corporation outstanding at the time the transaction commenced`           IS A NUMBER
    `the votes of the outstanding stock owned by persons who are directors and also officers`                      IS A NUMBER
    `of those votes, the votes owned by the interested stockholder (directors and officers)`                       IS A NUMBER
    `the votes of the outstanding stock owned by employee stock plans in which employee participants do not have the right to determine confidentially whether shares held subject to the plan will be tendered in a tender or exchange offer` IS A NUMBER
    `of those votes, the votes owned by the interested stockholder (employee stock plans)`                         IS A NUMBER
    `at or subsequent to such time the business combination is approved by the board of directors`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the business combination is authorized at an annual or special meeting of stockholders`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the business combination is authorized by written consent`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the votes in favor of the business combination (the affirmative vote) of the outstanding voting stock which is not owned by the interested stockholder` IS A NUMBER
    `the votes of the outstanding voting stock which is not owned by the interested stockholder`                  IS A NUMBER

-- (a)(1): prior to such time the board approved either the business combination or the transaction which resulted in the stockholder becoming an interested stockholder.
-- src:637 | Prior to such time the board of directors of the corporation approved either the business combination or the transaction which resulted in the stockholder becoming an interested stockholder;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(a)(1) (src:637)
GIVEN f IS A `s 203(a) Facts about a business combination with an interested stockholder`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(a)(1) the board of directors approved before that time` f MEANS
        f's `prior to such time the board of directors approved the business combination`
    OR  f's `prior to such time the board of directors approved the transaction which resulted in the stockholder becoming an interested stockholder`

-- The percentage of the voting stock that a number of votes represents (subsection (c)(8), last sentence: a percentage of voting stock is a percentage of the votes).
-- NOTHING when the votes of the voting stock are 0 or less, or the number of votes is below 0.
-- src:662 | Every reference to a percentage of voting stock shall refer to such percentage of the votes of such voting stock.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(8) (src:662)
GIVEN votes IS A NUMBER
      `the votes of the voting stock` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 203(c)(8) the percentage of the voting stock that the votes represent` votes `the votes of the voting stock` MEANS
    IF     (`the votes of the voting stock` GREATER THAN 0)
       AND (votes AT LEAST 0)
    THEN JUST (votes DIVIDED BY `the votes of the voting stock`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (a)(2): upon consummation of the transaction which resulted in the stockholder becoming an interested stockholder, the interested stockholder owned at least 85% of the voting stock outstanding
-- at the time the transaction commenced, excluding for determining the voting stock outstanding (but not the outstanding voting stock owned by the interested stockholder) those shares owned
-- (i) by persons who are directors and also officers and (ii) by employee stock plans in which participants do not have the right to determine confidentially whether shares held subject to the plan will be tendered.
-- src:638 | Upon consummation of the transaction which resulted in the stockholder becoming an interested stockholder, the interested stockholder owned at least 85% of the voting stock of the corporation outstanding at the time the transaction commenced, excluding for purposes of determining the voting stock outstanding (but not the outstanding voting stock owned by the interested stockholder) those shares owned (i) by persons who are directors and also officers and (ii) employee stock plans in which employee participants do not have the right to determine confidentially whether shares held subject to the plan will be tendered in a tender or exchange offer; or
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(a)(2) (src:638)
GIVEN f IS A `s 203(a) Facts about a business combination with an interested stockholder`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(a)(2) the interested stockholder owned at least 85% of the voting stock outstanding` f MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 203(c)(8) the percentage of the voting stock that the votes represent` (f's `the votes of the voting stock that the interested stockholder owned upon consummation of the transaction`) (`the votes of the voting stock counted as outstanding for subsection (a)(2)` f)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST share THEN JUST (share AT LEAST 85%)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(a)(2) (src:638)
GIVEN f IS A `s 203(a) Facts about a business combination with an interested stockholder`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the votes of the voting stock counted as outstanding for subsection (a)(2)` f MEANS
    (f's `the votes of the voting stock of the corporation outstanding at the time the transaction commenced`)
      MINUS ((f's `the votes of the outstanding stock owned by persons who are directors and also officers`) MINUS (f's `of those votes, the votes owned by the interested stockholder (directors and officers)`))
      MINUS ((f's `the votes of the outstanding stock owned by employee stock plans in which employee participants do not have the right to determine confidentially whether shares held subject to the plan will be tendered in a tender or exchange offer`) MINUS (f's `of those votes, the votes owned by the interested stockholder (employee stock plans)`))

-- (a)(3): at or subsequent to such time the business combination is approved by the board and authorized at an annual or special meeting of stockholders, and not by written consent,
-- by the affirmative vote of at least 66 2/3% of the outstanding voting stock which is not owned by the interested stockholder.
-- src:639 | At or subsequent to such time the business combination is approved by the board of directors and authorized at an annual or special meeting of stockholders, and not by written consent, by the affirmative vote of at least 66 2/3% of the outstanding voting stock which is not owned by the interested stockholder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(a)(3) (src:639)
GIVEN f IS A `s 203(a) Facts about a business combination with an interested stockholder`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(a)(3) the business combination was approved and authorized by the required vote` f MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vote carries` (`at least` ((200 DIVIDED BY 3)%) `of` (`another base named in the provision` OF "the outstanding voting stock which is not owned by the interested stockholder")) (f's `the votes in favor of the business combination (the affirmative vote) of the outstanding voting stock which is not owned by the interested stockholder`) (f's `the votes of the outstanding voting stock which is not owned by the interested stockholder`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST carried THEN
        JUST (    f's `at or subsequent to such time the business combination is approved by the board of directors`
              AND f's `the business combination is authorized at an annual or special meeting of stockholders`
              AND (NOT f's `the business combination is authorized by written consent`)
              AND carried)

-- Subsection (a): the corporation shall not engage in the business combination for 3 years following the time the stockholder became an interested stockholder, unless (1), (2) or (3).
-- The 3 years run from the day the stockholder became one and include the day that ends them (Fork F10). A business combination before that day, or after the 3 years, is not barred by this subsection.
-- NOTHING when an exception cannot be worked out (the vote counts or the outstanding stock are not usable) and no other exception settles the matter.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(a) (src:636)
GIVEN f IS A `s 203(a) Facts about a business combination with an interested stockholder`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(a) the corporation is barred from engaging in the business combination` f MEANS
    IF NOT (    ((f's `the day of the business combination`) AT LEAST (f's `the day the stockholder became an interested stockholder`))
            AND ((f's `the day of the business combination`) AT MOST (`the date` (`period in years` 3) `after` (f's `the day the stockholder became an interested stockholder`))))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE (IF `s 203(a)(1) the board of directors approved before that time` f
          THEN JUST FALSE
          ELSE (CONSIDER `s 203(a)(2) the interested stockholder owned at least 85% of the voting stock outstanding` f
                WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
                WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
                    (CONSIDER `s 203(a)(3) the business combination was approved and authorized by the required vote` f
                     WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
                     WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
                     WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING)
                WHEN NOTHING THEN
                    (CONSIDER `s 203(a)(3) the business combination was approved and authorized by the required vote` f
                     WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
                     WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
                     WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING)))

§ `Section 203(b): when the restrictions do not apply`

-- (b)(1): the corporation's original certificate of incorporation contains a provision expressly electing not to be governed by this section.
-- src:641 | The corporation’s original certificate of incorporation contains a provision expressly electing not to be governed by this section;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(1) (src:641)
GIVEN `the original certificate of incorporation contains a provision expressly electing not to be governed by section 203` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(b)(1) the restrictions do not apply because the original certificate elects out` `the original certificate of incorporation contains a provision expressly electing not to be governed by section 203` MEANS
    `the original certificate of incorporation contains a provision expressly electing not to be governed by section 203`

-- (b)(2): the corporation, by action of its board of directors, adopts an amendment to its bylaws within 90 days of February 2, 1988, expressly electing not to be governed by this section,
-- which amendment shall not be further amended by the board of directors. "Within 90 days of" is read as within 90 days before or after (Fork F12).
-- src:642 | The corporation, by action of its board of directors, adopts an amendment to its bylaws within 90 days of February 2, 1988, expressly electing not to be governed by this section, which amendment shall not be further amended by the board of directors;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(2) (src:642)
GIVEN `the day the board of directors adopted an amendment to the bylaws expressly electing not to be governed by section 203, if it did` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(b)(2) the restrictions do not apply because the board adopted a bylaw election in 1988` `the day the board of directors adopted an amendment to the bylaws expressly electing not to be governed by section 203, if it did` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the board of directors adopted an amendment to the bylaws expressly electing not to be governed by section 203, if it did`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST adopted THEN
            (    (adopted AT LEAST (`the date` (`period in days` 90) `before` `s 203(b)(2) the day the section is dated from for the 1988 bylaw election`))
             AND (adopted AT MOST (`the date` (`period in days` 90) `after` `s 203(b)(2) the day the section is dated from for the 1988 bylaw election`)))

-- src:642 | which amendment shall not be further amended by the board of directors;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(2) (src:642)
GIVEN `the bylaw amendment was adopted by the board of directors pursuant to paragraph (b)(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(b)(2) the board of directors is barred from further amending the bylaw amendment` `the bylaw amendment was adopted by the board of directors pursuant to paragraph (b)(2)` MEANS
    `the bylaw amendment was adopted by the board of directors pursuant to paragraph (b)(2)`

-- (b)(3): the corporation, by action of its stockholders, adopts an amendment to its certificate of incorporation or bylaws expressly electing not to be governed by this section,
-- adopted, in addition to any other vote required by law, by the affirmative vote of a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote thereon.
-- src:643 | The corporation, by action of its stockholders, adopts an amendment to its certificate of incorporation or bylaws expressly electing not to be governed by this section; provided that, in addition to any other vote required by law, such amendment to the certificate of incorporation or bylaws must be adopted by the affirmative vote of a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote thereon. In the case of a corporation that both (i) has never had a class of voting stock that falls within any of the 2 categories set out in paragraph (b)(4) of this section, and (ii) has not elected by a provision in its original certificate of incorporation or any amendment thereto to be governed by this section, such amendment shall become effective upon (i) in the case of an amendment to the certificate of incorporation, the date and time at which the certificate filed in accordance with § 103 of this title becomes effective thereunder or (ii) in the case of an amendment to the bylaws, the date of the adoption of such amendment. In all other cases, an amendment adopted pursuant to this paragraph shall become effective (i) in the case of an amendment to the certificate of incorporation, 12 months after the date and time at which the certificate filed in accordance with § 103 of this title becomes effective thereunder or (ii) in the case of an amendment to the bylaws, 12 months after the date of the adoption of such amendment, and, in either case, the election not to be governed by this section shall not apply to any business combination between such corporation and any person who became an interested stockholder of such corporation on or before (A) in the case of an amendment to the certificate of incorporation, the date and time at which the certificate filed in accordance with § 103 of this title becomes effective thereunder; or (B) in the case of an amendment to the bylaws, the date of the adoption of such amendment. A bylaw amendment adopted pursuant to this paragraph shall not be further amended by the board of directors;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(3) (src:643)
DECLARE `s 203(b)(3) Which instrument the stockholders amended` IS ONE OF
    `the certificate of incorporation under s 203(b)(3)`
    `the bylaws under s 203(b)(3)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(3) (src:643)
DECLARE `s 203(b)(3) Facts about an election by the stockholders` HAS
    `the instrument amended`                                                                                        IS A `s 203(b)(3) Which instrument the stockholders amended`
    `the votes in favor of the amendment`                                                                           IS A NUMBER
    `the outstanding stock entitled to vote thereon, in votes`                                                      IS A NUMBER
    `the greater vote required by any other law, if any`                                                            IS A MAYBE `Vote requirement`
    `the corporation has never had a class of voting stock that falls within either of the 2 categories set out in paragraph (b)(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation has not elected by a provision in its original certificate of incorporation or any amendment to be governed by section 203` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1): the day and time the certificate becomes effective
    `the day the amendment takes effect under section 103 (certificate) or the day it was adopted (bylaws)`          IS A DATE

-- The vote: a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote, or any greater vote that other law requires (both must be met: a "greater" requirement that is not greater leaves the majority in force; Fork F21).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(3) (src:643)
GIVEN e IS A `s 203(b)(3) Facts about an election by the stockholders`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(b)(3) the stockholders adopted the amendment by the required vote` e MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) (e's `the votes in favor of the amendment`) (e's `the outstanding stock entitled to vote thereon, in votes`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST majority THEN
        (CONSIDER e's `the greater vote required by any other law, if any`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST majority
         WHEN JUST greater THEN
             (CONSIDER `the vote carries` greater (e's `the votes in favor of the amendment`) (e's `the outstanding stock entitled to vote thereon, in votes`)
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
              WHEN JUST g THEN JUST (majority AND g)))

-- "In either case" in the last clause is read as the two cases (i) certificate amendment and (ii) bylaw amendment within "all other cases", so the exclusion of persons who became interested stockholders on or before the amendment day applies only where the amendment takes effect 12 months later (Fork F18).
-- When the amendment takes effect. In the case of a corporation that both (i) has never had a class of voting stock that falls within either category of paragraph (b)(4) and
-- (ii) has not elected by a provision in its original certificate or any amendment to be governed by this section, the amendment becomes effective on the day the certificate amendment becomes effective under section 103
-- or, for a bylaw amendment, on the day of its adoption. In all other cases it becomes effective 12 months after that day.
-- src:643 | In the case of a corporation that both (i) has never had a class of voting stock that falls within any of the 2 categories set out in paragraph (b)(4) of this section, and (ii) has not elected by a provision in its original certificate of incorporation or any amendment thereto to be governed by this section, such amendment shall become effective upon (i) in the case of an amendment to the certificate of incorporation, the date and time at which the certificate filed in accordance with § 103 of this title becomes effective thereunder or (ii) in the case of an amendment to the bylaws, the date of the adoption of such amendment. In all other cases, an amendment adopted pursuant to this paragraph shall become effective (i) in the case of an amendment to the certificate of incorporation, 12 months after the date and time at which the certificate filed in accordance with § 103 of this title becomes effective thereunder or (ii) in the case of an amendment to the bylaws, 12 months after the date of the adoption of such amendment, and, in either case, the election not to be governed by this section shall not apply to any business combination between such corporation and any person who became an interested stockholder of such corporation on or before (A) in the case of an amendment to the certificate of incorporation, the date and time at which the certificate filed in accordance with § 103 of this title becomes effective thereunder; or (B) in the case of an amendment to the bylaws, the date of the adoption of such amendment. A bylaw amendment adopted pursuant to this paragraph shall not be further amended by the board of directors;
-- src:643 | In all other cases, an amendment adopted pursuant to this paragraph shall become effective (i) in the case of an amendment to the certificate of incorporation, 12 months after the date and time at which the certificate filed in accordance with § 103 of this title becomes effective thereunder or (ii) in the case of an amendment to the bylaws, 12 months after the date of the adoption of such amendment, and, in either case, the election not to be governed by this section shall not apply to any business combination between such corporation and any person who became an interested stockholder of such corporation on or before (A) in the case of an amendment to the certificate of incorporation, the date and time at which the certificate filed in accordance with § 103 of this title becomes effective thereunder; or (B) in the case of an amendment to the bylaws, the date of the adoption of such amendment. A bylaw amendment adopted pursuant to this paragraph shall not be further amended by the board of directors;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(3) (src:643)
GIVEN e IS A `s 203(b)(3) Facts about an election by the stockholders`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 203(b)(3) the day from which the election not to be governed takes effect` e MEANS
    IF     e's `the corporation has never had a class of voting stock that falls within either of the 2 categories set out in paragraph (b)(4)`
       AND e's `the corporation has not elected by a provision in its original certificate of incorporation or any amendment to be governed by section 203`
    THEN e's `the day the amendment takes effect under section 103 (certificate) or the day it was adopted (bylaws)`
    ELSE `the date` (`period in months` 12) `after` (e's `the day the amendment takes effect under section 103 (certificate) or the day it was adopted (bylaws)`)

-- In the delayed case the election not to be governed shall not apply to any business combination between the corporation and any person who became an interested stockholder on or before
-- the day of the certificate amendment's effectiveness or the bylaw amendment's adoption. In either case the election is not in effect before the day from which it takes effect.
-- src:643 | and, in either case, the election not to be governed by this section shall not apply to any business combination between such corporation and any person who became an interested stockholder of such corporation on or before (A) in the case of an amendment to the certificate of incorporation, the date and time at which the certificate filed in accordance with § 103 of this title becomes effective thereunder; or (B) in the case of an amendment to the bylaws, the date of the adoption of such amendment. A bylaw amendment adopted pursuant to this paragraph shall not be further amended by the board of directors;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(3) (src:643)
GIVEN e IS A `s 203(b)(3) Facts about an election by the stockholders`
      `the day of the business combination` IS A DATE
      `the day the person became an interested stockholder` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(b)(3) the restrictions do not apply because of the stockholders' election` e `the day of the business combination` `the day the person became an interested stockholder` MEANS
        (    CONSIDER `s 203(b)(3) the stockholders adopted the amendment by the required vote` e
             WHEN JUST adopted THEN adopted
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
    AND (`the day of the business combination` AT LEAST (`s 203(b)(3) the day from which the election not to be governed takes effect` e))
    AND (    (    e's `the corporation has never had a class of voting stock that falls within either of the 2 categories set out in paragraph (b)(4)`
              AND e's `the corporation has not elected by a provision in its original certificate of incorporation or any amendment to be governed by section 203`)
         OR  (`the day the person became an interested stockholder` GREATER THAN (e's `the day the amendment takes effect under section 103 (certificate) or the day it was adopted (bylaws)`)))

-- src:643 | A bylaw amendment adopted pursuant to this paragraph shall not be further amended by the board of directors;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(3) (src:643)
GIVEN `the bylaw amendment was adopted by the stockholders pursuant to paragraph (b)(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(b)(3) the board of directors is barred from further amending the bylaw amendment` `the bylaw amendment was adopted by the stockholders pursuant to paragraph (b)(3)` MEANS
    `the bylaw amendment was adopted by the stockholders pursuant to paragraph (b)(3)`

-- The "unless" clause is read as disregarding a listing or a holder count that results from an interested stockholder's action, so the corporation is treated as having no such class and stays outside the section (Fork F17).
-- (b)(4): the corporation does not have a class of voting stock that is (i) listed on a national securities exchange or (ii) held of record by more than 2,000 stockholders,
-- unless any of the foregoing results from action taken, directly or indirectly, by an interested stockholder or from a transaction in which a person becomes an interested stockholder.
-- src:644 | The corporation does not have a class of voting stock that is: (i) Listed on a national securities exchange; or (ii) held of record by more than 2,000 stockholders, unless any of the foregoing results from action taken, directly or indirectly, by an interested stockholder or from a transaction in which a person becomes an interested stockholder;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(4) (src:644)
DECLARE `s 203(b)(4) Facts about the classes of voting stock` HAS
    -- out of range: the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (what a national securities exchange is): a stated fact
    `a class of voting stock is listed on a national securities exchange`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `that listing results from action taken, directly or indirectly, by an interested stockholder or from a transaction in which a person becomes an interested stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of stockholders of record of the class of voting stock with the most holders`                       IS A NUMBER
    `that number results from action taken, directly or indirectly, by an interested stockholder or from a transaction in which a person becomes an interested stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(4) (src:644)
GIVEN c IS A `s 203(b)(4) Facts about the classes of voting stock`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(b)(4) the restrictions do not apply because the corporation has no listed or widely held class of voting stock` c MEANS
        (NOT (    c's `a class of voting stock is listed on a national securities exchange`
              AND (NOT c's `that listing results from action taken, directly or indirectly, by an interested stockholder or from a transaction in which a person becomes an interested stockholder`)))
    AND (NOT (    (c's `the number of stockholders of record of the class of voting stock with the most holders`) GREATER THAN 2000
              AND (NOT c's `that number results from action taken, directly or indirectly, by an interested stockholder or from a transaction in which a person becomes an interested stockholder`)))

-- (b)(5): a stockholder becomes an interested stockholder inadvertently and (i) as soon as practicable divests itself of ownership of sufficient shares so that it ceases to be an interested stockholder; and
-- (ii) would not, at any time within the 3-year period immediately prior to a business combination between the corporation and the stockholder, have been an interested stockholder but for the inadvertent acquisition of ownership.
-- "As soon as practicable" is a judgment: an input.
-- src:645 | A stockholder becomes an interested stockholder inadvertently and (i) as soon as practicable divests itself of ownership of sufficient shares so that the stockholder ceases to be an interested stockholder; and (ii) would not, at any time within the 3-year period immediately prior to a business combination between the corporation and such stockholder, have been an interested stockholder but for the inadvertent acquisition of ownership;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(5) (src:645)
GIVEN `the stockholder became an interested stockholder inadvertently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder as soon as practicable divested itself of ownership of sufficient shares so that it ceased to be an interested stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder would not, at any time within the 3-year period immediately prior to the business combination, have been an interested stockholder but for the inadvertent acquisition of ownership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(b)(5) the restrictions do not apply because the stockholder became an interested stockholder inadvertently` `the stockholder became an interested stockholder inadvertently` `the stockholder as soon as practicable divested itself of ownership of sufficient shares so that it ceased to be an interested stockholder` `the stockholder would not, at any time within the 3-year period immediately prior to the business combination, have been an interested stockholder but for the inadvertent acquisition of ownership` MEANS
        `the stockholder became an interested stockholder inadvertently`
    AND `the stockholder as soon as practicable divested itself of ownership of sufficient shares so that it ceased to be an interested stockholder`
    AND `the stockholder would not, at any time within the 3-year period immediately prior to the business combination, have been an interested stockholder but for the inadvertent acquisition of ownership`

-- (b)(6): the business combination is proposed prior to the consummation or abandonment of, and subsequent to the earlier of the public announcement or the notice required hereunder of, a proposed transaction which
-- (i) is 1 of the transactions in the second sentence of the paragraph: (x) a merger or consolidation of the corporation (except for a merger for which, pursuant to section 251(f), no vote of the stockholders is required);
-- (y) a sale, lease, exchange, mortgage, pledge, transfer or other disposition of assets of the corporation or of a majority-owned subsidiary (other than to a wholly-owned subsidiary or to the corporation)
-- having an aggregate market value equal to 50% or more of either the aggregate market value of all the assets of the corporation on a consolidated basis or of all the outstanding stock; or (z) a proposed tender or exchange offer for 50% or more of the outstanding voting stock;
-- (ii) is with or by a person who either was not an interested stockholder during the previous 3 years or became one with the approval of the board or during the period described in paragraph (b)(7); and
-- (iii) is approved or not opposed by a majority of the members of the board then in office (but not less than 1) who were directors prior to any person becoming an interested stockholder during the previous 3 years or were recommended for election or elected to succeed such directors by a majority of such directors.
-- src:646 | The business combination is proposed prior to the consummation or abandonment of and subsequent to the earlier of the public announcement or the notice required hereunder of a proposed transaction which (i) constitutes 1 of the transactions described in the second sentence of this paragraph; (ii) is with or by a person who either was not an interested stockholder during the previous 3 years or who became an interested stockholder with the approval of the corporation’s board of directors or during the period described in paragraph (b)(7) of this section; and (iii) is approved or not opposed by a majority of the members of the board of directors then in office (but not less than 1) who were directors prior to any person becoming an interested stockholder during the previous 3 years or were recommended for election or elected to succeed such directors by a majority of such directors. The proposed transactions referred to in the preceding sentence are limited to (x) a merger or consolidation of the corporation (except for a merger in respect of which, pursuant to § 251(f) of this title, no vote of the stockholders of the corporation is required); (y) a sale, lease, exchange, mortgage, pledge, transfer or other disposition (in 1 transaction or a series of transactions), whether as part of a dissolution or otherwise, of assets of the corporation or of any direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary of the corporation (other than to any direct or indirect wholly-owned subsidiary or to the corporation) having an aggregate market value equal to 50% or more of either that aggregate market value of all of the assets of the corporation determined on a consolidated basis or the aggregate market value of all the outstanding stock of the corporation; or (z) a proposed tender or exchange offer for 50% or more of the outstanding voting stock of the corporation. The corporation shall give not less than 20 days’ notice to all interested stockholders prior to the consummation of any of the transactions described in clause (x) or (y) of the second sentence of this paragraph; or
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(6) (src:646)
DECLARE `s 203(b)(6) The proposed transaction` IS ONE OF
    `a merger or consolidation of the corporation under s 203(b)(6)(x)` HAS `no vote of the stockholders of the corporation is required pursuant to section 251(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a disposition of assets under s 203(b)(6)(y)` HAS
        `it is a sale, lease, exchange, mortgage, pledge, transfer or other disposition of assets of the corporation or of a direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
        `it is to a direct or indirect wholly-owned subsidiary or to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the aggregate market value of the assets disposed of` IS A NUMBER
        `the aggregate market value of all the assets of the corporation determined on a consolidated basis` IS A NUMBER
        `the aggregate market value of all the outstanding stock of the corporation` IS A NUMBER
    `a tender or exchange offer under s 203(b)(6)(z)` HAS
        `the votes of the outstanding voting stock of the corporation that the offer is for` IS A NUMBER
        `the votes of the outstanding voting stock of the corporation` IS A NUMBER
    `another transaction under s 203(b)(6)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(6) (src:646)
GIVEN t IS A `s 203(b)(6) The proposed transaction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(b)(6)(i) the proposed transaction is 1 of those the paragraph lists` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation of the corporation under s 203(b)(6)(x)` noVote THEN JUST (NOT noVote)
    WHEN `a disposition of assets under s 203(b)(6)(y)` disposition toSubsidiary valueOfAssets consolidated stockValue THEN
        JUST (    disposition
              AND (NOT toSubsidiary)
              AND (    (valueOfAssets AT LEAST (50% TIMES consolidated))
                   OR  (valueOfAssets AT LEAST (50% TIMES stockValue))))
    WHEN `a tender or exchange offer under s 203(b)(6)(z)` sought outstanding THEN
        (CONSIDER `s 203(c)(8) the percentage of the voting stock that the votes represent` sought outstanding
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST share THEN JUST (share AT LEAST 50%))
    WHEN `another transaction under s 203(b)(6)` THEN JUST FALSE

-- Facts about the timing of the proposal and about the person, for paragraph (b)(6).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(6) (src:646)
DECLARE `s 203(b)(6) Facts about the proposal and the person` HAS
    `the day the business combination is proposed`                                                              IS A DATE
    `the day of the public announcement of the proposed transaction, if any`                                    IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day of the notice required hereunder of the proposed transaction, if any`                              IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day the proposed transaction is consummated or abandoned, if it has been`                              IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the person was not an interested stockholder during the previous 3 years`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person became an interested stockholder with the approval of the corporation's board of directors`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person became an interested stockholder during the period described in paragraph (b)(7)`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of members of the board then in office who were directors prior to any person becoming an interested stockholder during the previous 3 years or were recommended for election or elected to succeed such directors by a majority of such directors` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of those members who approved or did not oppose the proposed transaction`                      IS A NUMBER

-- The proposal comes after the earlier of the announcement and the notice, and before the consummation or abandonment (if it has happened).
-- "Subsequent to" and "prior to" are read strictly: a proposal on the day of the announcement, the notice, or the consummation is not inside the window (Fork F20).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(6) (src:646)
GIVEN p IS A `s 203(b)(6) Facts about the proposal and the person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(b)(6) the business combination is proposed within the time the paragraph allows` p MEANS
        (    CONSIDER p's `the day of the public announcement of the proposed transaction, if any`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN
                 (CONSIDER p's `the day of the notice required hereunder of the proposed transaction, if any`
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                  WHEN JUST notice THEN ((p's `the day the business combination is proposed`) GREATER THAN notice))
             WHEN JUST announced THEN
                 (CONSIDER p's `the day of the notice required hereunder of the proposed transaction, if any`
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN ((p's `the day the business combination is proposed`) GREATER THAN announced)
                  WHEN JUST notice THEN ((p's `the day the business combination is proposed`) GREATER THAN (IF announced AT MOST notice THEN announced ELSE notice))))
    AND (    CONSIDER p's `the day the proposed transaction is consummated or abandoned, if it has been`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
             WHEN JUST ended THEN ((p's `the day the business combination is proposed`) LESS THAN ended))

@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(6) (src:646)
GIVEN p IS A `s 203(b)(6) Facts about the proposal and the person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(b)(6)(ii) the transaction is with or by a person of the kind the paragraph describes` p MEANS
        p's `the person was not an interested stockholder during the previous 3 years`
    OR  p's `the person became an interested stockholder with the approval of the corporation's board of directors`
    OR  p's `the person became an interested stockholder during the period described in paragraph (b)(7)`

-- (iii): approved or not opposed by a majority of the members of the board then in office (but not less than 1) who were directors prior to any person becoming an interested stockholder.
-- "Not less than 1" is read as requiring at least one of those members to have approved or not opposed (Fork F14).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(6) (src:646)
GIVEN p IS A `s 203(b)(6) Facts about the proposal and the person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(b)(6)(iii) the transaction is approved or not opposed by the required majority of the continuing directors` p MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vote carries` (`a majority of` (`another base named in the provision` OF "the members of the board then in office who were directors prior to any person becoming an interested stockholder during the previous 3 years or were recommended for election or elected to succeed such directors by a majority of such directors")) (p's `the number of those members who approved or did not oppose the proposed transaction`) (p's `the number of members of the board then in office who were directors prior to any person becoming an interested stockholder during the previous 3 years or were recommended for election or elected to succeed such directors by a majority of such directors`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST majority THEN JUST (majority AND ((p's `the number of those members who approved or did not oppose the proposed transaction`) AT LEAST 1))

-- All of (b)(6): proposed within the time, the transaction is of a listed kind, with a person of the described kind, approved or not opposed by the continuing directors.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(6) (src:646)
GIVEN t IS A `s 203(b)(6) The proposed transaction`
      p IS A `s 203(b)(6) Facts about the proposal and the person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(b)(6) the restrictions do not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` t p MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 203(b)(6)(i) the proposed transaction is 1 of those the paragraph lists` t
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST listed THEN
        (CONSIDER `s 203(b)(6)(iii) the transaction is approved or not opposed by the required majority of the continuing directors` p
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST approved THEN
             JUST (    `s 203(b)(6) the business combination is proposed within the time the paragraph allows` p
                   AND listed
                   AND `s 203(b)(6)(ii) the transaction is with or by a person of the kind the paragraph describes` p
                   AND approved))

-- The corporation shall give not less than 20 days' notice to all interested stockholders prior to the consummation of any of the transactions described in clause (x) or (y).
-- src:646 | The corporation shall give not less than 20 days’ notice to all interested stockholders prior to the consummation of any of the transactions described in clause (x) or (y) of the second sentence of this paragraph; or
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(6) (src:646)
GIVEN t IS A `s 203(b)(6) The proposed transaction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(b)(6) the corporation must give notice to all interested stockholders` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation of the corporation under s 203(b)(6)(x)` noVote THEN (NOT noVote)
    WHEN `a disposition of assets under s 203(b)(6)(y)` disposition toSubsidiary valueOfAssets consolidated stockValue THEN
        (    disposition
         AND (NOT toSubsidiary)
         AND (    (valueOfAssets AT LEAST (50% TIMES consolidated))
              OR  (valueOfAssets AT LEAST (50% TIMES stockValue))))
    WHEN `a tender or exchange offer under s 203(b)(6)(z)` sought outstanding THEN FALSE
    WHEN `another transaction under s 203(b)(6)` THEN FALSE

@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(6) (src:646)
GIVEN `the day the notice was given to the interested stockholders` IS A DATE
      `the day the transaction is consummated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(b)(6) the notice to the interested stockholders is timely` `the day the notice was given to the interested stockholders` `the day the transaction is consummated` MEANS
    `the day the notice was given to the interested stockholders` AT MOST (`the date` (`period in days` 20) `before` `the day the transaction is consummated`)

-- (b)(7): the business combination is with an interested stockholder who became one at a time when the restrictions did not apply by reason of any of paragraphs (b)(1) through (4),
-- provided that this paragraph does not apply if, at the time the stockholder became an interested stockholder, the certificate of incorporation contained a provision authorized by the last sentence of the subsection.
-- src:647 | The business combination is with an interested stockholder who became an interested stockholder at a time when the restrictions contained in this section did not apply by reason of any of paragraphs (b)(1) through (4) of this section, provided, however, that this paragraph (b)(7) shall not apply if, at the time such interested stockholder became an interested stockholder, the corporation’s certificate of incorporation contained a provision authorized by the last sentence of this subsection (b).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b)(7) (src:647)
GIVEN `the restrictions did not apply when the stockholder became an interested stockholder, by reason of any of paragraphs (b)(1) through (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at that time the certificate of incorporation contained a provision authorized by the last sentence of subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(b)(7) the restrictions do not apply because the stockholder became an interested stockholder when they did not apply` `the restrictions did not apply when the stockholder became an interested stockholder, by reason of any of paragraphs (b)(1) through (4)` `at that time the certificate of incorporation contained a provision authorized by the last sentence of subsection (b)` MEANS
        `the restrictions did not apply when the stockholder became an interested stockholder, by reason of any of paragraphs (b)(1) through (4)`
    AND (NOT `at that time the certificate of incorporation contained a provision authorized by the last sentence of subsection (b)`)

-- The last paragraph of subsection (b): notwithstanding paragraphs (b)(1) to (4), a corporation may elect by a provision of its original certificate or any amendment to be governed by the section;
-- but an amendment to the certificate shall not apply to restrict a business combination with an interested stockholder who became one before the day and time the amendment becomes effective.
-- src:648 | Notwithstanding paragraphs (b)(1), (2), (3) and (4) of this section, a corporation may elect by a provision of its original certificate of incorporation or any amendment thereto to be governed by this section; provided that any such amendment to the certificate of incorporation shall not apply to restrict a business combination between the corporation and an interested stockholder of the corporation if the interested stockholder became such before the date and time at which the certificate filed in accordance with § 103 of this title becomes effective thereunder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b) (src:648)
GIVEN `the corporation elected by a provision of its original certificate of incorporation to be governed by section 203` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation elected by an amendment to its certificate of incorporation to be governed by section 203` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1): the day and time the amendment becomes effective
      `the day the amendment electing to be governed becomes effective under section 103, if there is one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the person became an interested stockholder` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(b) the corporation's election to be governed applies to the interested stockholder` `the corporation elected by a provision of its original certificate of incorporation to be governed by section 203` `the corporation elected by an amendment to its certificate of incorporation to be governed by section 203` `the day the amendment electing to be governed becomes effective under section 103, if there is one` `the day the person became an interested stockholder` MEANS
        `the corporation elected by a provision of its original certificate of incorporation to be governed by section 203`
    OR  (    `the corporation elected by an amendment to its certificate of incorporation to be governed by section 203`
         AND (    CONSIDER `the day the amendment electing to be governed becomes effective under section 103, if there is one`
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                  WHEN JUST effective THEN (`the day the person became an interested stockholder` AT LEAST effective)))

-- Subsection (b) as a whole: the restrictions do not apply if any of paragraphs (b)(1) to (4) holds and the corporation has not elected to be governed, or if (b)(5), (b)(6) or (b)(7) holds.
-- NOTHING when paragraph (b)(6) cannot be worked out and the others do not settle the matter.
-- src:640 | (b) The restrictions contained in this section shall not apply if:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(b) (src:640)
GIVEN `paragraph (b)(1) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b)(2) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b)(3) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b)(4) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation's election to be governed applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b)(5) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b)(6) holds` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b)(7) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(b) the restrictions contained in this section do not apply` `paragraph (b)(1) holds` `paragraph (b)(2) holds` `paragraph (b)(3) holds` `paragraph (b)(4) holds` `the corporation's election to be governed applies` `paragraph (b)(5) holds` `paragraph (b)(6) holds` `paragraph (b)(7) holds` MEANS
    IF     (    (    `paragraph (b)(1) holds` OR `paragraph (b)(2) holds` OR `paragraph (b)(3) holds` OR `paragraph (b)(4) holds`)
            AND (NOT `the corporation's election to be governed applies`))
       OR  `paragraph (b)(5) holds`
       OR  `paragraph (b)(7) holds`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `paragraph (b)(6) holds`

§ `Section 203(c): definitions that apply to this section only`

-- (c)(1): "Affiliate" means a person that directly, or indirectly through 1 or more intermediaries, controls, or is controlled by, or is under common control with, another person.
-- src:650 | “Affiliate” means a person that directly, or indirectly through 1 or more intermediaries, controls, or is controlled by, or is under common control with, another person.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(1) (src:650)
GIVEN `the person controls the other person, directly or indirectly through 1 or more intermediaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is controlled by the other person, directly or indirectly through 1 or more intermediaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is under common control with the other person, directly or indirectly through 1 or more intermediaries` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(c)(1) the person is an affiliate of the other person` `the person controls the other person, directly or indirectly through 1 or more intermediaries` `the person is controlled by the other person, directly or indirectly through 1 or more intermediaries` `the person is under common control with the other person, directly or indirectly through 1 or more intermediaries` MEANS
        `the person controls the other person, directly or indirectly through 1 or more intermediaries`
    OR  `the person is controlled by the other person, directly or indirectly through 1 or more intermediaries`
    OR  `the person is under common control with the other person, directly or indirectly through 1 or more intermediaries`

-- (c)(2): "Associate", when used to indicate a relationship with any person, means (i) any corporation, partnership, unincorporated association or other entity of which that person is a director, officer or partner
-- or is, directly or indirectly, the owner of 20% or more of any class of voting stock; (ii) any trust or other estate in which that person has at least a 20% beneficial interest or as to which that person serves as trustee or in a similar fiduciary capacity;
-- and (iii) any relative or spouse of that person, or any relative of that spouse, who has the same residence as that person.
-- src:651 | “Associate,” when used to indicate a relationship with any person, means: (i) Any corporation, partnership, unincorporated association or other entity of which such person is a director, officer or partner or is, directly or indirectly, the owner of 20% or more of any class of voting stock; (ii) any trust or other estate in which such person has at least a 20% beneficial interest or as to which such person serves as trustee or in a similar fiduciary capacity; and (iii) any relative or spouse of such person, or any relative of such spouse, who has the same residence as such person.
-- src:651 | (i) Any corporation, partnership, unincorporated association or other entity of which such person is a director, officer or partner or is, directly or indirectly, the owner of 20% or more of any class of voting stock; (ii) any trust or other estate in which such person has at least a 20% beneficial interest or as to which such person serves as trustee or in a similar fiduciary capacity; and (iii) any relative or spouse of such person, or any relative of such spouse, who has the same residence as such person.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(2) (src:651)
DECLARE `s 203(c)(2) What the other party is to the person` IS ONE OF
    `a corporation, partnership, unincorporated association or other entity under s 203(c)(2)(i)` HAS
        `the person is a director, officer or partner of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the votes of a class of voting stock of the entity that the person owns, directly or indirectly` IS A NUMBER
        `the votes of that class of voting stock` IS A NUMBER
    `a trust or other estate under s 203(c)(2)(ii)` HAS
        `the person's beneficial interest in the trust or estate, as a fraction of the whole` IS A NUMBER
        `the person serves as trustee or in a similar fiduciary capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a relative or spouse of the person, or a relative of that spouse, under s 203(c)(2)(iii)` HAS
        `the other party has the same residence as the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `anything else under s 203(c)(2)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(2) (src:651)
GIVEN o IS A `s 203(c)(2) What the other party is to the person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(c)(2) the other party is an associate of the person` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `a corporation, partnership, unincorporated association or other entity under s 203(c)(2)(i)` officer owned classVotes THEN
        (IF officer
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE (CONSIDER `s 203(c)(8) the percentage of the voting stock that the votes represent` owned classVotes
               WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
               WHEN JUST share THEN JUST (share AT LEAST 20%)))
    WHEN `a trust or other estate under s 203(c)(2)(ii)` interest trustee THEN JUST (trustee OR (interest AT LEAST 20%))
    WHEN `a relative or spouse of the person, or a relative of that spouse, under s 203(c)(2)(iii)` sameResidence THEN JUST sameResidence
    WHEN `anything else under s 203(c)(2)` THEN JUST FALSE

-- (c)(3): "Business combination", when used in reference to any corporation and any interested stockholder of the corporation, means any of the five kinds of transaction in (i) to (v).
-- src:652 | “Business combination,” when used in reference to any corporation and any interested stockholder of such corporation, means:
-- src:653 | (i) Any merger or consolidation of the corporation or any direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary of the corporation with (A) the interested stockholder, or (B) with any other corporation, partnership, unincorporated association or other entity if the merger or consolidation is caused by the interested stockholder and as a result of such merger or consolidation subsection (a) of this section is not applicable to the surviving entity;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(3)(i) (src:653)
DECLARE `s 203(c)(3)(i) A merger or consolidation` HAS
    `it is a merger or consolidation of the corporation or of a direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is with the interested stockholder`                                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is with any other corporation, partnership, unincorporated association or other entity`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is caused by the interested stockholder`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `as a result of it subsection (a) is not applicable to the surviving entity`                                  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(3)(i) (src:653)
GIVEN m IS A `s 203(c)(3)(i) A merger or consolidation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(c)(3)(i) the merger or consolidation is a business combination` m MEANS
        m's `it is a merger or consolidation of the corporation or of a direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary of the corporation`
    AND (    m's `it is with the interested stockholder`
         OR  (    m's `it is with any other corporation, partnership, unincorporated association or other entity`
              AND m's `it is caused by the interested stockholder`
              AND m's `as a result of it subsection (a) is not applicable to the surviving entity`))

-- src:654 | (ii) Any sale, lease, exchange, mortgage, pledge, transfer or other disposition (in 1 transaction or a series of transactions), except proportionately as a stockholder of such corporation, to or with the interested stockholder, whether as part of a dissolution or otherwise, of assets of the corporation or of any direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary of the corporation which assets have an aggregate market value equal to 10% or more of either the aggregate market value of all the assets of the corporation determined on a consolidated basis or the aggregate market value of all the outstanding stock of the corporation;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(3)(ii) (src:654)
DECLARE `s 203(c)(3)(ii) A disposition of assets` HAS
    `it is a sale, lease, exchange, mortgage, pledge, transfer or other disposition of assets of the corporation or of a direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary of the corporation, in 1 transaction or a series of transactions, whether as part of a dissolution or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is to or with the interested stockholder`                                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is made proportionately as a stockholder of the corporation`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the aggregate market value of the assets`                                                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the aggregate market value of all the assets of the corporation determined on a consolidated basis`          IS A NUMBER
    `the aggregate market value of all the outstanding stock of the corporation`                                  IS A NUMBER

@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(3)(ii) (src:654)
GIVEN d IS A `s 203(c)(3)(ii) A disposition of assets`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(c)(3)(ii) the disposition of assets is a business combination` d MEANS
        d's `it is a sale, lease, exchange, mortgage, pledge, transfer or other disposition of assets of the corporation or of a direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary of the corporation, in 1 transaction or a series of transactions, whether as part of a dissolution or otherwise`
    AND d's `it is to or with the interested stockholder`
    AND (NOT d's `it is made proportionately as a stockholder of the corporation`)
    AND (    ((d's `the aggregate market value of the assets`) AT LEAST (10% TIMES (d's `the aggregate market value of all the assets of the corporation determined on a consolidated basis`)))
         OR  ((d's `the aggregate market value of the assets`) AT LEAST (10% TIMES (d's `the aggregate market value of all the outstanding stock of the corporation`))))

-- src:655 | (iii) Any transaction which results in the issuance or transfer by the corporation or by any direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary of the corporation of any stock of the corporation or of such subsidiary to the interested stockholder, except: (A) Pursuant to the exercise, exchange or conversion of securities exercisable for, exchangeable for or convertible into stock of such corporation or any such subsidiary which securities were outstanding prior to the time that the interested stockholder became such; (B) pursuant to a merger under § 251(g) of this title; (C) pursuant to a dividend or distribution paid or made, or the exercise, exchange or conversion of securities exercisable for, exchangeable for or convertible into stock of such corporation or any such subsidiary which security is distributed, pro rata to all holders of a class or series of stock of such corporation subsequent to the time the interested stockholder became such; (D) pursuant to an exchange offer by the corporation to purchase stock made on the same terms to all holders of said stock; or (E) any issuance or transfer of stock by the corporation; provided however, that in no case under items (C)-(E) of this subparagraph shall there be an increase in the interested stockholder’s proportionate share of the stock of any class or series of the corporation or of the voting stock of the corporation;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(3)(iii) (src:655)
DECLARE `s 203(c)(3)(iii) An issuance or transfer of stock` HAS
    `it results in the issuance or transfer by the corporation or by a direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary of any stock of the corporation or of the subsidiary to the interested stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is pursuant to the exercise, exchange or conversion of securities exercisable for, exchangeable for or convertible into stock which were outstanding prior to the time that the interested stockholder became such` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is pursuant to a merger under section 251(g)`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is pursuant to a dividend or distribution, or the exercise, exchange or conversion of securities distributed, pro rata to all holders of a class or series of stock subsequent to the time the interested stockholder became such` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is pursuant to an exchange offer by the corporation to purchase stock made on the same terms to all holders of that stock` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an issuance or transfer of stock by the corporation`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it increases the interested stockholder's proportionate share of the stock of any class or series of the corporation or of the voting stock of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(3)(iii) (src:655)
GIVEN i IS A `s 203(c)(3)(iii) An issuance or transfer of stock`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(c)(3)(iii) the issuance or transfer of stock is a business combination` i MEANS
        i's `it results in the issuance or transfer by the corporation or by a direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary of any stock of the corporation or of the subsidiary to the interested stockholder`
    AND (NOT (    i's `it is pursuant to the exercise, exchange or conversion of securities exercisable for, exchangeable for or convertible into stock which were outstanding prior to the time that the interested stockholder became such`
              OR  i's `it is pursuant to a merger under section 251(g)`
              OR  (    (    i's `it is pursuant to a dividend or distribution, or the exercise, exchange or conversion of securities distributed, pro rata to all holders of a class or series of stock subsequent to the time the interested stockholder became such`
                       OR  i's `it is pursuant to an exchange offer by the corporation to purchase stock made on the same terms to all holders of that stock`
                       OR  i's `it is an issuance or transfer of stock by the corporation`)
                   AND (NOT i's `it increases the interested stockholder's proportionate share of the stock of any class or series of the corporation or of the voting stock of the corporation`))))

-- src:656 | (iv) Any transaction involving the corporation or any direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary of the corporation which has the effect, directly or indirectly, of increasing the proportionate share of the stock of any class or series, or securities convertible into the stock of any class or series, of the corporation or of any such subsidiary which is owned by the interested stockholder, except as a result of immaterial changes due to fractional share adjustments or as a result of any purchase or redemption of any shares of stock not caused, directly or indirectly, by the interested stockholder; or
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(3)(iv) (src:656)
DECLARE `s 203(c)(3)(iv) A transaction increasing the interested stockholder's share` HAS
    `it involves the corporation or a direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary of the corporation and has the effect, directly or indirectly, of increasing the proportionate share of the stock of any class or series, or securities convertible into the stock of any class or series, owned by the interested stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the increase is the result of immaterial changes due to fractional share adjustments`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the increase is the result of a purchase or redemption of shares of stock not caused, directly or indirectly, by the interested stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(3)(iv) (src:656)
GIVEN t IS A `s 203(c)(3)(iv) A transaction increasing the interested stockholder's share`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(c)(3)(iv) the transaction increasing the interested stockholder's share is a business combination` t MEANS
        t's `it involves the corporation or a direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary of the corporation and has the effect, directly or indirectly, of increasing the proportionate share of the stock of any class or series, or securities convertible into the stock of any class or series, owned by the interested stockholder`
    AND (NOT (    t's `the increase is the result of immaterial changes due to fractional share adjustments`
              OR  t's `the increase is the result of a purchase or redemption of shares of stock not caused, directly or indirectly, by the interested stockholder`))

-- src:657 | (v) Any receipt by the interested stockholder of the benefit, directly or indirectly (except proportionately as a stockholder of such corporation), of any loans, advances, guarantees, pledges or other financial benefits (other than those expressly permitted in paragraphs (c)(3)(i)-(iv) of this section) provided by or through the corporation or any direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(3)(v) (src:657)
DECLARE `s 203(c)(3)(v) A receipt of a financial benefit` HAS
    `the interested stockholder receives the benefit, directly or indirectly, of loans, advances, guarantees, pledges or other financial benefits provided by or through the corporation or a direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is received proportionately as a stockholder of the corporation`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is expressly permitted in paragraphs (c)(3)(i) to (iv)`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(3)(v) (src:657)
GIVEN b IS A `s 203(c)(3)(v) A receipt of a financial benefit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(c)(3)(v) the receipt of a financial benefit is a business combination` b MEANS
        b's `the interested stockholder receives the benefit, directly or indirectly, of loans, advances, guarantees, pledges or other financial benefits provided by or through the corporation or a direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary`
    AND (NOT b's `it is received proportionately as a stockholder of the corporation`)
    AND (NOT b's `it is expressly permitted in paragraphs (c)(3)(i) to (iv)`)

-- The five kinds of transaction, one rule that asks the right limb.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(3) (src:652)
DECLARE `s 203(c)(3) A transaction with an interested stockholder` IS ONE OF
    `a merger or consolidation under s 203(c)(3)(i)` HAS `the facts of the merger or consolidation` IS A `s 203(c)(3)(i) A merger or consolidation`
    `a disposition of assets under s 203(c)(3)(ii)` HAS `the facts of the disposition of assets` IS A `s 203(c)(3)(ii) A disposition of assets`
    `an issuance or transfer of stock under s 203(c)(3)(iii)` HAS `the facts of the issuance or transfer of stock` IS A `s 203(c)(3)(iii) An issuance or transfer of stock`
    `a transaction increasing the interested stockholder's share under s 203(c)(3)(iv)` HAS `the facts of the transaction increasing the interested stockholder's share` IS A `s 203(c)(3)(iv) A transaction increasing the interested stockholder's share`
    `a receipt of a financial benefit under s 203(c)(3)(v)` HAS `the facts of the receipt of a financial benefit` IS A `s 203(c)(3)(v) A receipt of a financial benefit`
    `a transaction of another kind under s 203(c)(3)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(3) (src:652)
GIVEN t IS A `s 203(c)(3) A transaction with an interested stockholder`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(c)(3) the transaction is a business combination` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 203(c)(3)(i)` m THEN `s 203(c)(3)(i) the merger or consolidation is a business combination` m
    WHEN `a disposition of assets under s 203(c)(3)(ii)` d THEN `s 203(c)(3)(ii) the disposition of assets is a business combination` d
    WHEN `an issuance or transfer of stock under s 203(c)(3)(iii)` i THEN `s 203(c)(3)(iii) the issuance or transfer of stock is a business combination` i
    WHEN `a transaction increasing the interested stockholder's share under s 203(c)(3)(iv)` x THEN `s 203(c)(3)(iv) the transaction increasing the interested stockholder's share is a business combination` x
    WHEN `a receipt of a financial benefit under s 203(c)(3)(v)` b THEN `s 203(c)(3)(v) the receipt of a financial benefit is a business combination` b
    WHEN `a transaction of another kind under s 203(c)(3)` THEN FALSE

-- (c)(4): "Control", including the terms "controlling", "controlled by" and "under common control with", means the possession, directly or indirectly, of the power to direct or cause the direction of the management
-- and policies of a person, whether through the ownership of voting stock, by contract or otherwise. A person who is the owner of 20% or more of the outstanding voting stock of any corporation, partnership, unincorporated association
-- or other entity shall be presumed to have control of such entity, in the absence of proof by a preponderance of the evidence to the contrary; but the presumption does not apply where the person holds voting stock, in good faith and not for the purpose
-- of circumventing this section, as an agent, bank, broker, nominee, custodian or trustee for 1 or more owners who do not individually or as a group have control of the entity.
-- Whether the presumption has been rebutted, and whether the holding is in good faith, are findings of someone else: inputs.
-- src:658 | “Control,” including the terms “controlling,” “controlled by” and “under common control with,” means the possession, directly or indirectly, of the power to direct or cause the direction of the management and policies of a person, whether through the ownership of voting stock, by contract or otherwise. A person who is the owner of 20% or more of the outstanding voting stock of any corporation, partnership, unincorporated association or other entity shall be presumed to have control of such entity, in the absence of proof by a preponderance of the evidence to the contrary; Notwithstanding the foregoing, a presumption of control shall not apply where such person holds voting stock, in good faith and not for the purpose of circumventing this section, as an agent, bank, broker, nominee, custodian or trustee for 1 or more owners who do not individually or as a group have control of such entity.
-- src:658 | A person who is the owner of 20% or more of the outstanding voting stock of any corporation, partnership, unincorporated association or other entity shall be presumed to have control of such entity, in the absence of proof by a preponderance of the evidence to the contrary; Notwithstanding the foregoing, a presumption of control shall not apply where such person holds voting stock, in good faith and not for the purpose of circumventing this section, as an agent, bank, broker, nominee, custodian or trustee for 1 or more owners who do not individually or as a group have control of such entity.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(4) (src:658)
DECLARE `s 203(c)(4) Facts about control of an entity` HAS
    `the person possesses, directly or indirectly, the power to direct or cause the direction of the management and policies of the entity, whether through the ownership of voting stock, by contract or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the votes of the outstanding voting stock of the entity that the person owns`                               IS A NUMBER
    `the votes of the outstanding voting stock of the entity`                                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the presumption of control is rebutted by proof by a preponderance of the evidence to the contrary`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person holds the voting stock in good faith and not for the purpose of circumventing section 203, as an agent, bank, broker, nominee, custodian or trustee for 1 or more owners who do not individually or as a group have control of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(4) (src:658)
GIVEN c IS A `s 203(c)(4) Facts about control of an entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(c)(4) the person has control of the entity` c MEANS
    IF c's `the person possesses, directly or indirectly, the power to direct or cause the direction of the management and policies of the entity, whether through the ownership of voting stock, by contract or otherwise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE (CONSIDER `s 203(c)(8) the percentage of the voting stock that the votes represent` (c's `the votes of the outstanding voting stock of the entity that the person owns`) (c's `the votes of the outstanding voting stock of the entity`)
          WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
          WHEN JUST share THEN
              JUST (    (share AT LEAST 20%)
                    AND (NOT c's `the presumption of control is rebutted by proof by a preponderance of the evidence to the contrary`)
                    AND (NOT c's `the person holds the voting stock in good faith and not for the purpose of circumventing section 203, as an agent, bank, broker, nominee, custodian or trustee for 1 or more owners who do not individually or as a group have control of the entity`)))

-- (c)(6): "Person" means any individual, corporation, partnership, unincorporated association or other entity: every kind of entity in dg-core's list is a person.
-- src:660 | “Person” means any individual, corporation, partnership, unincorporated association or other entity.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(6) (src:660)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(c)(6) the kind of entity is a person` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a natural person` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a corporation` kindOfCorporation THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- (c)(7): "Stock" means, with respect to any corporation, capital stock and, with respect to any other entity, any equity interest.
-- An individual is not an entity that issues stock: NOTHING.
-- src:661 | “Stock” means, with respect to any corporation, capital stock and, with respect to any other entity, any equity interest.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(7) (src:661)
GIVEN issuer IS A `Kind of entity`
      `the interest is capital stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest is an equity interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(c)(7) the interest is stock` issuer `the interest is capital stock` `the interest is an equity interest` MEANS
    CONSIDER issuer
    WHEN `a natural person` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a corporation` kindOfCorporation THEN JUST `the interest is capital stock`
    OTHERWISE JUST `the interest is an equity interest`

-- (c)(8): "Voting stock" means, with respect to any corporation, stock of any class or series entitled to vote generally in the election of directors and, with respect to any entity that is not a corporation,
-- any equity interest entitled to vote generally in the election of the governing body of the entity. (The sentence on percentages is encoded above, beside subsection (a)(2).)
-- src:662 | “Voting stock” means, with respect to any corporation, stock of any class or series entitled to vote generally in the election of directors and, with respect to any entity that is not a corporation, any equity interest entitled to vote generally in the election of the governing body of such entity. Every reference to a percentage of voting stock shall refer to such percentage of the votes of such voting stock.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(8) (src:662)
GIVEN issuer IS A `Kind of entity`
      `the stock is of a class or series entitled to vote generally in the election of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equity interest is entitled to vote generally in the election of the governing body of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(c)(8) the interest is voting stock` issuer `the stock is of a class or series entitled to vote generally in the election of directors` `the equity interest is entitled to vote generally in the election of the governing body of the entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER issuer
    WHEN `a natural person` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a corporation` kindOfCorporation THEN JUST `the stock is of a class or series entitled to vote generally in the election of directors`
    OTHERWISE JUST `the equity interest is entitled to vote generally in the election of the governing body of the entity`

-- (c)(9): "Owner", including "own" and "owned", when used with respect to any stock, means a person that individually or with or through any of its affiliates or associates:
-- (i) beneficially owns such stock, directly or indirectly; or (ii) has (A) the right to acquire such stock (whether exercisable immediately or only after the passage of time) pursuant to any agreement, arrangement or understanding,
-- or upon the exercise of conversion rights, exchange rights, warrants or options, or otherwise; provided that a person shall not be deemed the owner of stock tendered pursuant to a tender or exchange offer made by such person or any of its affiliates
-- or associates until such tendered stock is accepted for purchase or exchange; or (B) the right to vote such stock pursuant to any agreement, arrangement or understanding; provided that a person shall not be deemed the owner of any stock because of such right
-- to vote if the agreement, arrangement or understanding arises solely from a revocable proxy or consent given in response to a proxy or consent solicitation made to 10 or more persons; or (iii) has any agreement, arrangement or understanding for the purpose of
-- acquiring, holding, voting (except voting pursuant to a revocable proxy or consent as described in item (B) of subparagraph (ii)) or disposing of such stock with any other person that beneficially owns, or whose affiliates or associates beneficially own, directly or indirectly, such stock.
-- src:663 | “Owner,” including the terms “own” and “owned,” when used with respect to any stock, means a person that individually or with or through any of its affiliates or associates:
-- src:664 | (i) Beneficially owns such stock, directly or indirectly; or
-- src:665 | (ii) Has (A) the right to acquire such stock (whether such right is exercisable immediately or only after the passage of time) pursuant to any agreement, arrangement or understanding, or upon the exercise of conversion rights, exchange rights, warrants or options, or otherwise; provided, however, that a person shall not be deemed the owner of stock tendered pursuant to a tender or exchange offer made by such person or any of such person’s affiliates or associates until such tendered stock is accepted for purchase or exchange; or (B) the right to vote such stock pursuant to any agreement, arrangement or understanding; provided, however, that a person shall not be deemed the owner of any stock because of such person’s right to vote such stock if the agreement, arrangement or understanding to vote such stock arises solely from a revocable proxy or consent given in response to a proxy or consent solicitation made to 10 or more persons; or
-- src:666 | (iii) Has any agreement, arrangement or understanding for the purpose of acquiring, holding, voting (except voting pursuant to a revocable proxy or consent as described in item (B) of subparagraph (ii) of this paragraph), or disposing of such stock with any other person that beneficially owns, or whose affiliates or associates beneficially own, directly or indirectly, such stock.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(9) (src:663-666)
DECLARE `s 203(c)(9) A block of voting stock` HAS
    `the votes of the block`                                                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `the block is outstanding`                                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person, individually or with or through its affiliates or associates, beneficially owns the block, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has the right to acquire the block`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the block is tendered pursuant to a tender or exchange offer made by the person or any of its affiliates or associates` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tendered block has been accepted for purchase or exchange`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has the right to vote the block pursuant to an agreement, arrangement or understanding`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `that agreement, arrangement or understanding arises solely from a revocable proxy or consent given in response to a solicitation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of persons to whom that solicitation was made`                                                   IS A NUMBER
    `the person has an agreement, arrangement or understanding for the purpose of acquiring, holding, voting or disposing of the block with another person that beneficially owns it`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the voting under that agreement is pursuant to a revocable proxy or consent as described in item (B) of subparagraph (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(9) (src:663-666)
GIVEN b IS A `s 203(c)(9) A block of voting stock`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(c)(9) the person is the owner of the block` b MEANS
        b's `the person, individually or with or through its affiliates or associates, beneficially owns the block, directly or indirectly`
    OR  (    b's `the person has the right to acquire the block`
         AND (NOT (    b's `the block is tendered pursuant to a tender or exchange offer made by the person or any of its affiliates or associates`
                   AND (NOT b's `the tendered block has been accepted for purchase or exchange`))))
    OR  (    b's `the person has the right to vote the block pursuant to an agreement, arrangement or understanding`
         AND (NOT (    b's `that agreement, arrangement or understanding arises solely from a revocable proxy or consent given in response to a solicitation`
                   AND ((b's `the number of persons to whom that solicitation was made`) AT LEAST 10))))
    OR  (    b's `the person has an agreement, arrangement or understanding for the purpose of acquiring, holding, voting or disposing of the block with another person that beneficially owns it`
         AND (NOT b's `the voting under that agreement is pursuant to a revocable proxy or consent as described in item (B) of subparagraph (ii)`))

-- The votes of the voting stock that the person owns: the votes of the blocks the person is the owner of.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(9) (src:663)
GIVEN blocks IS A LIST OF `s 203(c)(9) A block of voting stock`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 203(c)(9) the votes of the voting stock that the person owns` blocks MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN b YIELD b's `the votes of the block`) (filter (GIVEN b YIELD `s 203(c)(9) the person is the owner of the block` b) blocks))

-- The votes of the owned blocks that are not yet outstanding (stock the person is deemed to own by paragraph (9)), which the last sentence of paragraph (5) counts as outstanding.
-- src:659 | For the purpose of determining whether a person is an interested stockholder, the voting stock of the corporation deemed to be outstanding shall include stock deemed to be owned by the person through application of paragraph (9) of this subsection but shall not include any other unissued stock of such corporation which may be issuable pursuant to any agreement, arrangement or understanding, or upon exercise of conversion rights, warrants or options, or otherwise.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(5) (src:659)
GIVEN blocks IS A LIST OF `s 203(c)(9) A block of voting stock`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 203(c)(5) the votes of owned stock that is not yet outstanding` blocks MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN b YIELD b's `the votes of the block`) (filter (GIVEN b YIELD `s 203(c)(9) the person is the owner of the block` b AND (NOT b's `the block is outstanding`)) blocks))

-- (c)(5): "Interested stockholder" means any person (other than the corporation and any direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary of the corporation) that (i) is the owner of 15% or more of the outstanding voting stock of the corporation, or
-- (ii) is an affiliate or associate of the corporation and was the owner of 15% or more of the outstanding voting stock at any time within the 3-year period immediately prior to the date on which it is sought to be determined whether the person is an interested stockholder,
-- and the affiliates and associates of such person; the term does not include (x) a person who (A) owned shares in excess of 15% as of, or acquired them pursuant to a tender offer commenced prior to, December 23, 1987, or pursuant to an exchange offer announced
-- prior to that date and commenced within 90 days thereafter, and either (I) continued to own shares in excess of 15% or would have but for action by the corporation or (II) is an affiliate or associate of the corporation and so continued, or (B) acquired the shares from a person described
-- in (A) by gift, inheritance or in a transaction in which no consideration was exchanged; or (y) a person whose ownership in excess of 15% is the result of action taken solely by the corporation, but such a person is an interested stockholder if thereafter it acquires additional shares of voting stock,
-- except as a result of further corporate action not caused, directly or indirectly, by it.
-- src:659 | “Interested stockholder” means any person (other than the corporation and any direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary of the corporation) that (i) is the owner of 15% or more of the outstanding voting stock of the corporation, or (ii) is an affiliate or associate of the corporation and was the owner of 15% or more of the outstanding voting stock of the corporation at any time within the 3-year period immediately prior to the date on which it is sought to be determined whether such person is an interested stockholder, and the affiliates and associates of such person; provided, however, that the term “interested stockholder” shall not include (x) any person who (A) owned shares in excess of the 15% limitation set forth herein as of, or acquired such shares pursuant to a tender offer commenced prior to, December 23, 1987, or pursuant to an exchange offer announced prior to the aforesaid date and commenced within 90 days thereafter and either (I) continued to own shares in excess of such 15% limitation or would have but for action by the corporation or (II) is an affiliate or associate of the corporation and so continued (or so would have continued but for action by the corporation) to be the owner of 15% or more of the outstanding voting stock of the corporation at any time within the 3-year period immediately prior to the date on which it is sought to be determined whether such a person is an interested stockholder or (B) acquired said shares from a person described in item (A) of this paragraph by gift, inheritance or in a transaction in which no consideration was exchanged; or (y) any person whose ownership of shares in excess of the 15% limitation set forth herein is the result of action taken solely by the corporation; provided that such person shall be an interested stockholder if thereafter such person acquires additional shares of voting stock of the corporation, except as a result of further corporate action not caused, directly or indirectly, by such person. For the purpose of determining whether a person is an interested stockholder, the voting stock of the corporation deemed to be outstanding shall include stock deemed to be owned by the person through application of paragraph (9) of this subsection but shall not include any other unissued stock of such corporation which may be issuable pursuant to any agreement, arrangement or understanding, or upon exercise of conversion rights, warrants or options, or otherwise.
-- src:659 | and the affiliates and associates of such person; provided, however, that the term “interested stockholder” shall not include (x) any person who (A) owned shares in excess of the 15% limitation set forth herein as of, or acquired such shares pursuant to a tender offer commenced prior to, December 23, 1987, or pursuant to an exchange offer announced prior to the aforesaid date and commenced within 90 days thereafter and either (I) continued to own shares in excess of such 15% limitation or would have but for action by the corporation or (II) is an affiliate or associate of the corporation and so continued (or so would have continued but for action by the corporation) to be the owner of 15% or more of the outstanding voting stock of the corporation at any time within the 3-year period immediately prior to the date on which it is sought to be determined whether such a person is an interested stockholder or (B) acquired said shares from a person described in item (A) of this paragraph by gift, inheritance or in a transaction in which no consideration was exchanged; or (y) any person whose ownership of shares in excess of the 15% limitation set forth herein is the result of action taken solely by the corporation; provided that such person shall be an interested stockholder if thereafter such person acquires additional shares of voting stock of the corporation, except as a result of further corporate action not caused, directly or indirectly, by such person. For the purpose of determining whether a person is an interested stockholder, the voting stock of the corporation deemed to be outstanding shall include stock deemed to be owned by the person through application of paragraph (9) of this subsection but shall not include any other unissued stock of such corporation which may be issuable pursuant to any agreement, arrangement or understanding, or upon exercise of conversion rights, warrants or options, or otherwise.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(5) (src:659)
DECLARE `s 203(c)(5) The facts that take a person out of the term` HAS
    `the person owned shares in excess of the 15% limitation as of December 23, 1987`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the tender offer was commenced, if the person acquired the shares pursuant to one`                  IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day the exchange offer was announced, if the person acquired the shares pursuant to one`                IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day the exchange offer was commenced, if the person acquired the shares pursuant to one`                IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the person continued to own shares in excess of the 15% limitation, or would have but for action by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is an affiliate or associate of the corporation and so continued to be the owner of 15% or more of the outstanding voting stock at any time within the 3-year period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person acquired the shares from a person described in item (A) by gift, inheritance or in a transaction in which no consideration was exchanged` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person's ownership of shares in excess of the 15% limitation is the result of action taken solely by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `thereafter the person acquired additional shares of voting stock of the corporation, other than as a result of further corporate action not caused, directly or indirectly, by the person` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(5) (src:659)
DECLARE `s 203(c)(5) Facts about a person and the corporation` HAS
    `the person is the corporation or a direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary of the corporation`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the votes of the voting stock of the corporation outstanding`                                               IS A NUMBER
    `the blocks of voting stock the person may be the owner of`                                                  IS A LIST OF `s 203(c)(9) A block of voting stock`
    `the person is an affiliate or associate of the corporation`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was the owner of 15% or more of the outstanding voting stock of the corporation at any time within the 3-year period immediately prior to the date it is sought to be determined whether the person is an interested stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is an affiliate or associate of a person who is an interested stockholder under item (i) or (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the exclusions`                                                                                             IS A `s 203(c)(5) The facts that take a person out of the term`

-- Item (A) of proviso (x): owned shares in excess of 15% as of December 23, 1987, or acquired them pursuant to a tender offer commenced before that day, or pursuant to an exchange offer announced before that day and commenced within 90 days after it;
-- and either (I) continued to own them or (II) is an affiliate or associate of the corporation and so continued.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(5) (src:659)
GIVEN x IS A `s 203(c)(5) The facts that take a person out of the term`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(c)(5)(x) the person is described in item (A) of the proviso` x MEANS
        (    x's `the person owned shares in excess of the 15% limitation as of December 23, 1987`
         OR  (    CONSIDER x's `the day the tender offer was commenced, if the person acquired the shares pursuant to one`
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                  WHEN JUST commenced THEN (commenced LESS THAN `s 203(c)(5) the day before which the 1987 tender offers and exchange offers must have begun`))
         OR  (    (    CONSIDER x's `the day the exchange offer was announced, if the person acquired the shares pursuant to one`
                       WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                       WHEN JUST announced THEN (announced LESS THAN `s 203(c)(5) the day before which the 1987 tender offers and exchange offers must have begun`))
              AND (    CONSIDER x's `the day the exchange offer was commenced, if the person acquired the shares pursuant to one`
                       WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                       WHEN JUST began THEN (began AT MOST (`the date` (`period in days` 90) `after` `s 203(c)(5) the day before which the 1987 tender offers and exchange offers must have begun`)))))
    AND (    x's `the person continued to own shares in excess of the 15% limitation, or would have but for action by the corporation`
         OR  x's `the person is an affiliate or associate of the corporation and so continued to be the owner of 15% or more of the outstanding voting stock at any time within the 3-year period`)

-- The term does not include a person described in (x) (item (A), or item (B): shares acquired from such a person by gift, inheritance or for no consideration)
-- or in (y) (ownership in excess of 15% resulting solely from the corporation's action, unless the person thereafter acquires additional shares other than by further corporate action not caused by it).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(5) (src:659)
GIVEN x IS A `s 203(c)(5) The facts that take a person out of the term`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 203(c)(5) the person is excluded from the term` x MEANS
        `s 203(c)(5)(x) the person is described in item (A) of the proviso` x
    OR  x's `the person acquired the shares from a person described in item (A) by gift, inheritance or in a transaction in which no consideration was exchanged`
    OR  (    x's `the person's ownership of shares in excess of the 15% limitation is the result of action taken solely by the corporation`
         AND (NOT x's `thereafter the person acquired additional shares of voting stock of the corporation, other than as a result of further corporate action not caused, directly or indirectly, by the person`))

-- Whether the person is an interested stockholder. The votes counted as outstanding include the votes of unissued stock the person is deemed to own by paragraph (9) and no other unissued stock.
-- NOTHING when the votes counted as outstanding are 0 or less.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(c)(5) (src:659)
GIVEN f IS A `s 203(c)(5) Facts about a person and the corporation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(c)(5) the person is an interested stockholder` f MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 203(c)(8) the percentage of the voting stock that the votes represent`
                 (`s 203(c)(9) the votes of the voting stock that the person owns` (f's `the blocks of voting stock the person may be the owner of`))
                 ((f's `the votes of the voting stock of the corporation outstanding`) PLUS (`s 203(c)(5) the votes of owned stock that is not yet outstanding` (f's `the blocks of voting stock the person may be the owner of`)))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST share THEN
        JUST (    (NOT f's `the person is the corporation or a direct or indirect majority-owned subsidiary of the corporation`)
              AND (    (share AT LEAST 15%)
                   OR  (    f's `the person is an affiliate or associate of the corporation`
                        AND f's `the person was the owner of 15% or more of the outstanding voting stock of the corporation at any time within the 3-year period immediately prior to the date it is sought to be determined whether the person is an interested stockholder`)
                   OR  f's `the person is an affiliate or associate of a person who is an interested stockholder under item (i) or (ii)`)
              AND (NOT `s 203(c)(5) the person is excluded from the term` (f's `the exclusions`)))

§ `Section 203(d) and (e): greater votes; jurisdiction`

-- Subsection (d): no provision of a certificate of incorporation or bylaw shall require, for any vote of stockholders required by this section, a greater vote of stockholders than that specified in this section.
-- A requirement is greater when its proportion is larger, or the same and it must be exceeded where the section's need only be reached. Requirements counted against different bases are not compared: NOTHING.
-- src:667 | No provision of a certificate of incorporation or bylaw shall require, for any vote of stockholders required by this section, a greater vote of stockholders than that specified in this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(d) (src:667)
GIVEN `the vote the provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaw requires` IS A `Vote requirement`
      `the vote this section specifies` IS A `Vote requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(d) the provision requires a greater vote than this section specifies` `the vote the provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaw requires` `the vote this section specifies` MEANS
    IF (`the vote the provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaw requires`'s `counted against`) EQUALS (`the vote this section specifies`'s `counted against`)
    THEN JUST (    ((`the vote the provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaw requires`'s proportion) GREATER THAN (`the vote this section specifies`'s proportion))
               OR  (    ((`the vote the provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaw requires`'s proportion) EQUALS (`the vote this section specifies`'s proportion))
                    AND (`the vote the provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaw requires`'s `must be exceeded`)
                    AND (NOT (`the vote this section specifies`'s `must be exceeded`))))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (e): the Court of Chancery is vested with exclusive jurisdiction to hear and determine all matters with respect to this section.
-- A matter that is not one with respect to this section is not covered: NOTHING.
-- src:668 | The Court of Chancery is hereby vested with exclusive jurisdiction to hear and determine all matters with respect to this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203(e) (src:668)
GIVEN court IS AN Actor
      `the matter is a matter with respect to section 203` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(e) the court has jurisdiction to hear and determine the matter` court `the matter is a matter with respect to section 203` MEANS
    IF `the matter is a matter with respect to section 203`
    THEN JUST (court EQUALS `the Court of Chancery`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 203: the whole`

-- Subsection (a) bars the business combination unless subsection (b) exempts the corporation or the combination (and it does not apply if an exception in (a) holds).
-- The corporation is barred if the restrictions apply and subsection (a) bars; NOTHING if either cannot be worked out and the other does not settle the matter.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 203 (src:636)
GIVEN `the restrictions contained in this section do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `subsection (a) bars the business combination` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203 the corporation may not engage in the business combination` `the restrictions contained in this section do not apply` `subsection (a) bars the business combination` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the restrictions contained in this section do not apply`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN `subsection (a) bars the business combination`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        (CONSIDER `subsection (a) bars the business combination`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING)
